{"name":"Forever","hex":"#bbe1e6","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Forever","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative form of forever."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Forever"}],"entries":[{"title":"Forever (1921 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Forever is a 1921 American silent romance film, also known as Peter Ibbetson, that was written by Ouida Bergère and directed by George Fitzmaurice. It was adapted from George du Maurier's 1891 novel Peter Ibbetson, which was made into a play of the same name by John N. Raphael."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b6/Forever-1921.jpg/330px-Forever-1921.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Forever_(1921_film)"},{"title":"Forever (1978 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Forever is a 1978 American made-for-television romantic drama film starring Stephanie Zimbalist and Dean Butler. It is based on the Judy Blume novel Forever... and premiered on CBS on January 6, 1978."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Forever_(1978_film)"},{"title":"Forever (2014 TV series)","blocks":[{"text":"Forever is an American fantasy crime drama television series that aired on ABC as part of the 2014–15 fall television season. Created by Matthew Miller, it centers on the character of Dr. Henry Morgan, an immortal New York City medical examiner who uses his extensive knowledge to assist the New York City Police Department (NYPD) in solving crimes and to discover a way to end his immortality. Flashbacks within each episode reveal various details of Henry's life."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/8/84/Forever_%28U.S._TV_series%29_Title_Card.png/330px-Forever_%28U.S._TV_series%29_Title_Card.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Forever_(2014_TV_series)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/c